      ],
      "schema:name": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Sales Tax (Amendment) Bill 2006"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_1",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "1",
      "hasPart": [
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_1__subsec_1",
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_1__subsec_2"
      ],
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_1__subsec_1",
      "@type": "akn:subsection",
      "eli:number": "1",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_1",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "This Act may be cited as the Sales Tax (Amendment) Act 2006."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_1__subsec_2",
      "@type": "akn:subsection",
      "eli:number": "2",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_1",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "This Act comes into operation on a date to be appointed by the Minister by notification in the Gazette, and the Minister may appoint different dates for the coming into operation of different provisions of this Act. Amendment of section 2"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_2",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "2",
      "hasPart": [
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_2__para_a",
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_2__para_b"
      ],
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The Sales Tax Act 1972 [Act 64], which is referred to as the \"principal Act\" in this Act, is amended in section 2 —"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_2__para_a",
      "@type": "akn:paragraph",
      "eli:number": "a",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_2",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "by inserting after the definition of \"customs\" the following definition: ' \"Customs Appeal Tribunal\" means the Customs Appeal Tribunal established under section 141B of the Customs Act 1967 [Act 235];'; and"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_2__para_b",
      "@type": "akn:paragraph",
      "eli:number": "b",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_2",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "by inserting after the definition of \"customs control\" the following definition: ' \"customs ruling\" means the customs ruling made by the Director General under section 11B;'. New Part IVA"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_3",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "3",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The principal Act is amended by inserting after section 11 the following Part: \"PART IVA CUSTOMS RULING Application for customs ruling 11A. (1) Any person may apply, in the prescribed form together with the prescribed fee, to the Director General for a customs ruling in respect of any one or more of the following matters: (a) the classification of goods; (b) the determination of a taxable person; (c) the principles to be adopted for the purposes of determination of value of goods; or (d) any other matters to be prescribed by the Director General. (2) An application under subsection (1) may be made — (a) in respect of imported goods — (i) at any time before the goods, that are the subject matter of the application, are to be imported or intended to be imported into Malaysia; or (ii) at any later time, if the Director General may in his discretion permit; or (b) in respect of manufactured goods — (i) at any time before the goods, that are the subject matter of the application, are to be manufactured; or Sales Tax (Amendment) (ii) at any later time, if the Director General may in his discretion permit. (3) An applicant may withdraw his application at any time before a customs ruling is made and any payment made relating to the application for the customs ruling shall be forfeited by the Director General. Making of customs ruling 11B. (1) Subject to subsection (3), the Director General shall make a customs ruling in respect of any matter specified in the application made under section 11A and such ruling shall bind the applicant. (2) Any such customs ruling may be subject to such conditions as the Director General may deem fit to impose. (3) The Director General may decline to make a customs ruling if, in his opinion — (a) the information given by the applicant is insufficient to do so; (b) the application is for a hypothetical situation; or (c) an appeal under this Act is pending involving the subject matter referred to in the application. Amendment, modification or revocation of customs ruling lie. (1) A customs ruling may be amended, modified or revoked by the Director General if— (a) it contains an error which needs to be corrected; (b) the customs ruling was based on an error of fact or law; (c) there is a change in law relating to sales tax; or (d) there is a change in the material fact or circumstances on which the ruling was based. (2) The Director General shall, immediately after making the amendment, modification or revocation, give a notice in writing to the applicant of the amendment, modification or revocation and, subject to subsection (3), such amended, modified or revoked customs ruling shall take effect from the date stated in the notice. (3) Notwithstanding subsection (2), where a customs ruling has the effect of causing or increasing any tax liability in respect of any goods, and — (a) the goods are imported within three months of the date the notice of the amendment, modification or revocation is given pursuant to a binding contract entered into before that date; (b) the goods have left the place of manufacture or warehouse in the country from which they are being exported for direct shipment to Malaysia on the date the notice of the amendment, modification or revocation of the ruling is given; or (c) the goods are imported on or before the date the notice of the amendment, modification or revocation is given but have not been released for the home consumption, then the customs ruling which was made prior to amendment, modification or revocation under this section shall be applied to such goods. (4) Notwithstanding subsection (2), and subject section 32, if the amendment, modification or revocation to a customs ruling has the effect of decreasing any tax liability in respect of any goods, any higher tax that has been paid shall been treated as if the higher tax paid in error. Director General to declare rulings to be null, etc. 11D. The Director General shall by a notice declare a customs ruling made under section 11B to be null, void and of no effect if the ruling has been obtained by the applicant by way of fraud, misrepresentation or falsification of facts. Sales Tax (Amendment) Receiving of two customs rulings HE. Where an applicant receives two or more different customs rulings on the same subject matter, such rulings shall be treated as being null and void and such applicant shall immediately notify the Director General who shall, within thirty days from the date of notification, issue a new customs ruling.\". New section 12B"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_4",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "4",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The principal Act is amended by inserting after section 12A the following section: \"Certificate under section 11B to be admissible 12B. Notwithstanding anything contained in any other written law or rule of evidence to the contrary, where in any proceedings a document purporting to be a certificate under the hand of the Director General in respect of a decision made by him under section 11B is produced, such document shall be admissible in evidence and shall be accepted as sufficient evidence of the facts therein stated and the Director General shall not be required to give evidence in respect of such decision unless the court otherwise orders.\". Amendment of section 61"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_5",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "5",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Section 61 of the principal Act is amended by inserting after paragraph (db) the following paragraphs: \"(dc) the conduct of all matters relating to customs rulings; (rr) the fees relating to customs rulings and the manner for collecting and disbursing such fees; (ss) the forms to be used for the purpose of customs rulings;\". Amendment of section 68"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_6",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "6",
      "hasPart": [
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_6__para_a",
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_6__para_b"
      ],
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@",
      "schema:name": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Section 68 of the principal Act is amended—"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_6__para_a",
      "@type": "akn:paragraph",
      "eli:number": "a",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_6",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "by substituting for subsection (2) the following subsection: \"(2) Any person aggrieved by a decision of the Director General may, except in any matter relating to compound or subsection 55(3), within thirty days of being notified of such decision in writing, appeal to the Customs Appeal Tribunal whose decision shall be final\"; and"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_6__para_b",
      "@type": "akn:paragraph",
      "eli:number": "b",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_6",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "by inserting after subsection (2) the following subsection: \"(3) All provisions relating to the Customs Appeal Tribunal shall be applicable to this Act.\". Saving and transitional"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_7",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "7",
      "hasPart": [
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_7__subsec_1",
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_7__subsec_2",
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_7__subsec_3",
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_7__subsec_4"
      ],
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_7__subsec_1",
      "@type": "akn:subsection",
      "eli:number": "1",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_7",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Notwithstanding section 3 of this Act, any customs ruling made by the Director General prior to the coming into operation of the section, is deemed to have been made under that section and valid for a period of three years from the date of coming into operation of such"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_7__subsec_2",
      "@type": "akn:subsection",
      "eli:number": "2",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_7",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Any appeal under paragraph 68(2)(a) of the principal Act to the court made before the appointed date and is pending on such date shall, after the appointed date, be continued as if the principal Act had not been amended by this Act."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_7__subsec_3",
      "@type": "akn:subsection",
      "eli:number": "3",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_7",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Any appeal under paragraph 68(2)(b) of the principal Act to the Minister made before the appointed date and is pending on such date shall, after the appointed date, be continued as if the principal Act had not been amended by this Act."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_7__subsec_4",
      "@type": "akn:subsection",
      "eli:number": "4",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2006/42/eng@/~cl_7",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "For the purpose of subsections (2) and (3), \"appointed date\" means the date appointed by the Minister under subsection 1(2)."
      }
    }
  ]
}
